          "distinct": false,
          "id": "604a37253820e50d1cdfaf26895b53a4d4fa2e56",
          "message": "ci: wire @jeswr/solid-server build+test + trusted-publish (sq-6xasp.11) [OPUS-4.8] (#2249)\n\nFinal CI plumbing for the WASM-Solid-server-on-npm epic (sq-6xasp). The package +\nOIDC host already landed (#2243/#2247); this adds the two workflow legs.\n\njs.yml: a build+test leg for packages/solid-server (working-directory scoped, same\nshape as the eyereasoner-compat leg) — `npm run build:lws-wasm` (crates/sparq-lws-wasm\nvia the wasm-pack already installed in the job) then `npm test` (node:test:\nhttp/auth/server/oidc, incl. the npx spin-up). The wasm build precedes the tests\nbecause src/index.js statically imports the wasm module, so the server/oidc tests\nfail module resolution without a built wasm/ tree. The existing `packages/**` +\n`crates/sparq-*-wasm/**` paths filter already covers these surfaces, and the root\n`npm ci` step already installs the package's workspace deps — no filter or install\nchange needed. The gating `js` check name is unchanged (no advisory/informational\ntoken), so the ci-summary / gate aggregator still treats it as a HARD required gate.\n\npublish.yml: a `npm-solid-server` OIDC trusted-publishing job mirroring the\n@sparq-org/eyereasoner-compat job — tokenless (id-token: write, no NPM_TOKEN),\nmanual `workflow_dispatch` only (never on `release: published`), builds the wasm\nexplicitly before publish (this package has no prepack/build hook), `npm publish\n--provenance --access public`, then verifies the registry recorded a provenance\nattestation. Includes the standard maintainer BOOTSTRAP comment (npm trusted\npublishing needs the package to already exist → one manual bootstrap publish, then\ntokenless).\n\nAll actions SHA-pinned (reused the existing pins; no new action introduced). Valid\nYAML + actionlint clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: GPT-5.6 <noreply@openai.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-13T08:23:04Z",
          "tree_id": "af852b7c84e054f59ea32d8edd924b253a2f187c",
